{"shortDescription":"The Australian dollar held its recent decline below $0.72, staying near its lowest in more than a week and on track for a weekly loss as the US dollar strengthened alongside a sharp rise in Treasury yields.The greenback gained after US producer inflation came in stronger, reinforcing expectations t…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Australian dollar held its recent decline below $0.72, staying near its lowest in more than a week and on track for a weekly loss as the US dollar strengthened alongside a sharp rise in Treasury yields."]},{"type":"p","children":["The greenback gained after US producer inflation came in stronger, reinforcing expectations that the Fed could raise rates next week."]},{"type":"p","children":["A sharp rise in Treasury yields also underpinned the dollar following lower-than-expected purchases by the US Treasury Department during its first expanded buyback operation."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, oil prices continued to rise above $100 per barrel amid the escalating Middle East tensions, raising inflation risks and expectations that central banks may keep policy tighter for longer."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets ramped up bets on a fourth rate hike this year by the Reserve Bank of Australia, with swaps now implying an 84% chance of a 25-bp increase at the upcoming meeting this month."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets also expect the cash rate to reach 4.85% by early next year, its highest level since 2008."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:582955:0","title":"Australian Dollar Set for Weekly Loss","published":1789090416,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/australia/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:AUDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/AU",